---
description: Python conventions for the latency predictor servers
globs:
  - "**/*.py"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Python 3.11+: use `StrEnum`, `X | None` unions, `datetime.now(UTC)`.
- Lint/format with ruff (`make lint`, `make fmt`); line length 120; rules E, W, F, I, UP.
- Pydantic v1-style API is intentionally in use (`.dict()`, `min_items`) — stay
  consistent; do not half-migrate to v2 idioms.
- Optional deps (xgboost, lightgbm, orjson) are guarded by try/except import
  with graceful fallback — preserve this pattern for any new optional dependency.
- Threading pattern: daemon threads with `threading.Event` shutdown signaling;
  snapshot shared state under the lock, do heavy work (joblib load, DataFrame
  build, inference) OUTSIDE the lock; hold locks only for pointer swaps.
- Feature engineering is duplicated in `training_server.py` and
  `prediction_server.py` (`_prepare_features_with_interaction`,
  `_prepare_features_for_ensemble`). Any change must be applied to BOTH files
  identically, keeping column names and order in sync.
- New config knobs = env vars with defaults in `PredictSettings`/`Settings`;
  document them in `docs/architecture.md`.
